This feature enables the OpenVINO NPU plugin on Intel x86 platforms.
It installs the Intel NPU driver (linux-npu-driver) and firmware, enables
the intel-npu kernel feature, and configures openvino-inference-engine
with NPU support.

This feature requires feature/openvino, see file "require".

To use this feature, add

    --templates feature/openvino-npu

The Compiler in Driver (CiD) is a set of C++ libraries designed for Intel Neural Processing
Unit (NPU) devices, providing a common API that allows the User Mode Driver to access compiler
functions through the vcl* interface methods.

How to build Compiler in Driver on target board.

	$ wget https://github.com/git-lfs/git-lfs/releases/download/v3.6.1/git-lfs-linux-amd64-v3.6.1.tar.gz
	$ tar -zxf git-lfs-linux-amd64-v3.6.1.tar.gz
	$ cd git-lfs-3.6.1
	$ cp git-lfs  /usr/bin

	$ git clone https://github.com/intel/linux-npu-driver.git
	$ cd linux-npu-driver
	$ git checkout tags/v1.28.0
	$ git submodule update --init --recursive
	$ cmake -B build -S . -DENABLE_NPU_COMPILER_BUILD=ON
	$ cd build
	$ make npu_compiler_source
	$ sed -i '/add_subdirectory(thirdparty EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL)/a \
	  add_compile_options(-Wno-error=maybe-uninitialized)\n\
	  add_compile_options(-Wno-error=stringop-overflow)\n\
	  add_compile_options(-Wno-error=dangling-reference)\n\
	  add_compile_options(-Wno-error=template-id-cdtor)' compiler/src/npu_compiler/CMakeLists.txt
	$ make openvino_source
	$ make npu_compiler_openvino_source
	$ sed -i '/#include <utility>/a #include <cstdint>' \
	  compiler/src/npu_compiler_openvino/thirdparty/gtest/gtest/googletest/src/gtest-death-test.cc
	$ make npu_compiler_build -j$(nproc)
	$ cp ./compiler/build_npu_compiler/bin/intel64/Release/libnpu_driver_compiler.so /lib64

#@TYPE: Wrtemplate
#@NAME: openvino-npu
#@DESCRIPTION: Enable OpenVINO NPU plugin with Intel NPU driver on intel-x86 platforms.
